  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The table below shows the relationship between the number of cars $c$ passing through a particular avenue in $m$ minutes.\n\n| Minutes ($m$) | Cars ($c$) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $15$ |\n| $5$ | $25$ |\n| $7$ | $42$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. There is a proportional relationship between $c$ and $m.$\n\nII. There is **not** a proportional relationship between $c$ and $m.$\n\nIII. The constant of proportionality is $11.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's add a new column to our table and compute the ratio of cars per minute for each row.\n\n| Minutes ($m$) | Cars ($c$) | Cars / Minutes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $15$ | $5$ |\n| $5$ | $25$ | $5$ |\n| $7$ | $42$ | $6$ |\n\nThe ratio of cars per minute is not the same for each row. Therefore, there is *not* a proportional relationship between $c$ and $m.$ Consequently, there is no constant of proportionality.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
